name issue_127_pacer_v2_jitter_reorder_loss
describe pacer v2 with rtx v2 on a 4 Mbps link with 30 ms jitter (reordering) and 2% loss: no repeated 2.5 s freezes (issue #139, #127)
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=4000kbps delay=40ms jitter=30ms loss=2% queue=150ms
# #139's repro. Before #159 (sequence number assigned at queue time) seeds 1-5 had longest freeze 2474-2612 ms,
# 20-47 keyframe requests and 1.2-9.4 % residual loss, because the pacer's keyframe flush
# (PacingController::EnqueuePacket) left sequence gaps that NACK chased until nack/abandon.
# libwebrtc numbers its packets when the pacer releases them (packet_router.cc:217), so a flush leaves no gap.
# Seeds 1-5 on main d2461d5 with `rtx v2`: longest freeze 220-392 ms, 1-4 keyframe requests, 0 % residual loss.
# sm_compare runs 40 seeds of both stacks here (#230): the freeze count is a rare-event count (sd 1.3-1.5 per seed),
# and 10 seeds gave a gap that 40 don't. Seeds 1-10: ours 3.3 / libwebrtc 1.1 freezes; seeds 1-40: 2.0 / 1.4
# (yardstick #274 at 59dfcf4, inside the parity band of +-0.7).
compare_seeds 40
expect video.longest_freeze_ms < 1000
expect video.keyframe_requests < 10
expect video.residual_loss_pct < 1
